MAC_EXIT=65 — DIAGNOSIS: no development signing certificate on the runner
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The macOS app targets carry entitlements (Resources/TeslaSync-macOS.entitlements) and the
project ships DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="" / CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Automatic. The runner has no signing
identity, so the macOS build fails at the signing stage (iOS Simulator builds are exempt,
which is why iOS reached the compile/test phase and macOS did not):
  error: "TeslaSync-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a development
         certificate. Enable development signing in the Signing & Capabilities editor.
  error: "TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a development
         certificate.
  ** TEST FAILED **  (1 failure)  — "Testing cancelled because the build failed."
This is an environmental/runner-config limitation. Note: macOS and iOS share ONE Sources/
group (ADR-002), already proven to compile by the iOS app build above.

